# Godot client

Canonical guidance: `docs/engineering/godot.md`. Runtime boundary: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. Version policy: `docs/engineering/VERSIONS.md`.

Godot displays projections and sends semantic input. It does not own authoritative inventory, money, relationships, ownership or outcomes.

Do:
- typed GDScript;
- reusable/independent scenes;
- parent-mediated wiring and semantic signals;
- InputMap actions;
- presentation interpolation separated from simulation time;
- restrained Autoload use;
- treat Resources as shared client-side data containers, not native world truth.

Do not:
- create Autoload `World` / authoritative `GameState`;
- mutate world truth directly from UI or animation callbacks;
- hardcode cross-scene `../../..` dependencies;
- use frame `delta` to advance the simulation;
- add C# gameplay because the editor is Mono-capable.

Inspect the current projection/adapter API before using it.
